Model Performance Summary (Part 1)
The classification task aimed to distinguish between nonspam and spam messages using Support Vector Machines (SVM) and Bernoulli Naive Bayes. The evaluation metrics show strong performance with a clear leaning toward effective spam detection.

✅ Key Metrics:

Accuracy: 82.74% – The model correctly classified the majority of messages.
AUC (Area Under ROC Curve): 0.9585 – Excellent separability between spam and nonspam.
F1 Score: 0.8383 – Balanced performance across precision and recall.
Kappa: 0.6604 – Substantial agreement beyond chance.
📌 Class-wise Performance:

Nonspam (Positive Class):
Sensitivity (Recall): 0.7380 – Some nonspam messages were misclassified as spam.
Negative Predictive Value (NPV): 0.7052 – Indicates missed detections of nonspam.
Spam:
Specificity: 0.9650 – The model very effectively identifies spam messages.
Precision: 0.9701 – Very few false positives among spam predictions.
📈 Highlights:

High AUC and specificity suggest the model is highly effective at catching spam while keeping false alarms low.
The slightly lower sensitivity on nonspam indicates room for improvement in avoiding misclassification of genuine messages.
